    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25xjkSizeFBrzHTULVxNtCU)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on current `main` (after #523 and #525); independent of #513 and #526.\n- Touches `sp-agenda-views.el` (via `sp-org-agenda.org`) and the inline test only.\n\n## What I found\n\n- The inline view (`C-c o x`, filter `C-c o X`) already had `sp-agenda-views-inline-extra-dirs`, but the default was only `sp-writing-projects`, so litnotes were not scanned.\n- The old hidden-folder check looked at the full path, so a folder under a hidden directory would have been skipped entirely.\n- Org's search view opens every file it scans, so adding hundreds of litnotes unfiltered would be slow.\n- The search view skips text before a file's first heading (confirmed in Emacs 29.3's `org-search-view`) and files with no heading. Litnotes can have text there.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Default `sp-agenda-views-inline-extra-dirs` is now `sp-writing-projects` plus `litnotes/` in `sp-notes-dir` (folders or single files). The whole notes folder is not a default: it is large and mostly PARA files the agenda already lists.\n- New `sp-agenda-views-inline-exclude-regexp`: skips hidden files and folders, lock and backup files, `archive/` and `backup/` folders, `.org_archive` files, matched against the path relative to each folder.\n- Ripgrep prefilter: of the extra files, only those that hold a keyword (case-insensitive, whole words, same filter as the view) are searched; 400 files per call. Agenda files are always searched. Without ripgrep, or if it fails, every extra file is searched.\n- The file list is built each time the view opens, so a new litnote shows without a restart.\n- New `sp-agenda-views-inline-grep` (`g` in the `C-c o X` menu): lists every keyword line in a grep buffer, including text before a file's first heading; `RET` jumps to the line. Needs ripgrep.\n- Filtered and unfiltered views both use the same file list.\n- Docs as bullets in `sp-org-agenda.org`, re-tangled. `CHANGELOG.org` not edited.\n\n## Checked by Claude\n\n- Emacs 29.3 batch: 15 ERT tests pass (the 9 earlier ones plus default dirs, exclusions, single file, prefilter with and without `rg`, file union).\n- `tools/check-tangle.sh`: all modules match their docs.\n- Not run: the view on your real litnotes (count, speed), the grep buffer in a GUI Emacs, jumping from a hit.\n\n## Not covered / open questions\n\n- Other folders worth adding yourself if you want them: the rest of `~/notes` (vulpea notes), `~/adr`. I left them out for size.\n- The search view shows an entry per heading, not per line; a `SOURCEREFS` line before the first heading only shows in the grep list.\n- Many open litnote buffers: the search view leaves the files it visited open, as before, now only the ones with a keyword.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `emacs -Q --batch -l ert -l tests/sp-agenda-views-inline-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` passes\n- [ ] Put `SOURCEREFS Smith 2017` under a heading of a litnote (not in the agenda); `C-c o x` lists it with the litnote title, and `RET` jumps to the entry\n- [ ] Put one before the first heading of a litnote: it is not in `C-c o x`, but `C-c o X`, `g` lists it in a grep buffer and `RET` jumps to the line\n- [ ] `C-c o X`, `f`, `SOURCEREFS`: only SOURCEREFS in both the view and the grep list; `c` clears\n- [ ] A `FIXME` in a file in `litnotes/archive/` or a `.org_archive` file is not listed\n- [ ] The view opens in about the same time as before with your full litnotes folder (note the time)\n- [ ] Create a new litnote with a keyword: it shows without restarting Emacs\n- [ ] `M-x customize-variable sp-agenda-views-inline-extra-dirs` shows the litnotes folder; adding a single file works\n- [ ] Regression: `C-c o a SPC`, `c` and `i i` still open\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9taQEBJAWpQmkyfLY)_",
